## API Specification

### Authentication (`/api/v1/auth`)
- `POST /register` -> Create account & send verification token
- `POST /login` -> Validate credentials, check MFA requirement, initiate session
- `POST /mfa/verify` -> Complete login with TOTP code
- `POST /mfa/recovery` -> Complete login using a single-use recovery code
- `POST /logout` -> Terminate current session & clear cookie
- `POST /logout-all` -> Revoke all active sessions for current user
- `POST /forgot-password` -> Request password reset email token
- `POST /reset-password` -> Reset password with token
- `GET /me` -> Get authenticated user profile & quota stats

### MFA Management (`/api/v1/mfa`)
- `POST /enable/init` -> Generate TOTP secret & QR code
- `POST /enable/confirm` -> Verify TOTP code, enable MFA, return recovery codes
- `POST /disable` -> Require password re-auth, then disable MFA

### File & Folder Operations (`/api/v1/files`, `/api/v1/folders`)
- `GET /folders` -> List folders in current parent
- `POST /folders` -> Create folder
- `PATCH /folders/:id` -> Rename / Move folder
- `DELETE /folders/:id` -> Move folder to trash / Permanent delete
- `GET /files` -> List files in folder / root
- `POST /files/upload` -> Multipart upload file (Quarantine -> Scan -> Encrypt -> MinIO)
- `GET /files/:id/download` -> Decrypt & stream file content
- `GET /files/:id` -> Get file metadata & details
- `PATCH /files/:id` -> Rename or move file
- `DELETE /files/:id` -> Soft delete (Move to trash)
- `POST /files/:id/restore` -> Restore file from trash
- `DELETE /files/:id/permanent` -> Secure shred key & delete from MinIO

### Sharing (`/api/v1/shares`)
- `POST /shares` -> Create secure share link for file/folder
- `GET /shares` -> List user's created share links
- `DELETE /shares/:id` -> Revoke share link
- `GET /public/share/:token` -> Fetch public share metadata
- `POST /public/share/:token/download` -> Validate share password/limits & download file

### Security & Audit (`/api/v1/security`)
- `GET /sessions` -> List active user sessions
- `DELETE /sessions/:id` -> Revoke specific session
- `GET /audit-logs` -> List paginated security audit history
- `POST /change-password` -> Re-authenticate & update password

